// Bari, Hegde, de Veciana's requests (arXiv 2508.01002): Poisson arrivals, a
// prompt of 1 .. vpmax whole tiles, an output of at most vdmax tokens
// (examples/papers/bari_rad.sq runs it).
use "std/args";

let tile = 128;  // b_col: a tile, in tokens (the server's `bcol`)
let vpmax = 8;  // prompts are 1 .. vpmax tiles (Assumption 3)
let vdmax = 512;  // the largest output
let rate = args.number("rate", 0.00002);  // requests per µs (20 per second)

// --8<-- [start:workload]
workload {
  arrive poisson(rate);
  init {
    set t0 = now;
    set vp = tile * floor(~uniform(1, vpmax + 1));
    set vd = min(floor(~exp(200)) + 1, vdmax);
  }
  send (vp, vd, t0);
}
// --8<-- [end:workload]
